---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { config } from "../lib/config.js";
---
<Base current="about" title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">{config.site.description}</p>
  <p>The site gathers India's macroeconomic, financial and market indicators from official public sources (MoSPI, the Reserve Bank of India, FBIL and others) into one place and updates them as new numbers are released. It is written for economists, students and anyone who wants the numbers with their sources.</p>
  <h2>Inspiration</h2>
  <p>{config.credit.inspired_by_text} <a href={config.credit.inspired_by_url}>{config.credit.inspired_by_url}</a></p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Automated pipelines download each release, check it against plausible ranges and the previously published values, and only then publish it. If a download fails, the site keeps the last good values and marks the series as stale. Every number on every page is drawn from a stored series; nothing is typed in by hand. Sources, coverage and licences are listed on the <a href="/data/">Data</a> page.</p>
  <p>Written briefings, when they arrive, will be drafted with AI from these data and reviewed by a person before publication.</p>
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with Econvitals, the Reserve Bank of India, the Government of India or any data provider.</p>
  <p class="chart-sub">This is a private preview; contact details and the corrections policy will be added before launch.</p>
</Base>
